  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1229 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nClosed upper low evident in water vapor imagery is centered over \nsouthern MN/northern IA. Further upstream, another closed low is \npushing into the Four Corners region. A surface low is centered \nacross northern WI/west-central MN with a secondary trough axis \nstretching back into SD. Low clouds and spotty light showers are \npushing through south-central SD along the northwestern periphery \nof the upper low; coverage and amounts will be limited. Precipitation\nchances taper off quickly this afternoon as the low pulls away. \nPatchy fog is possible across northwestern SD into north- central \nSD tonight after 06-08z; CAMs continue to show potential (REFS\nprob of visibility < 3 miles ~50-70%) for widespread fog in this \narea.\n\nMild and dry weather continues through the week with even warmer \nweather for the weekend into early next week as upper ridge builds. \nLooking at high temperatures Saturday through Monday of 10F+ above \nnormal. Expect elevated fire weather conditions given warm and dry \nweather coupled with breezy winds through Monday. A quick moving \nclipper will drop through the region late Friday with breezy NW \nwinds Saturday across northwestern SD (gusts 25 to 35 mph). No \nprecipitation on the horizon, at least through the middle of next \nweek.",
